## The word list is not covered by the above

`content/lexicon/en-frequency.txt` is not mine to relicense. It derives from
the Google Web Trillion Word Corpus (LDC2006T13) by way of Peter Norvig's
subsets and Josh Kaufman's `google-10000-english`, and it reaches you under
those terms rather than under the MIT licence above: educational and
personal/research use is permitted, and commercial use is not recommended
without licensing the corpus from the Linguistic Data Consortium.

The full chain of provenance, the exact wording of that permission, and the
filtering applied to the list are recorded in `content/lexicon/SOURCE.md`.
Read it before shipping anything commercial that keeps this file — the rest of
the pipeline does not depend on it, and rebuilding the word ordering from a
public-domain frequency list would put the whole repository under the MIT
licence with nothing carved out.

`content/lexicon/en-ru-frequency.jsonl` is a different matter: it is the output
of running the word list through this project's own prompt, no third-party
translation set is involved, and it carries no obligation from anyone else.
